WITH incoming AS (
  SELECT * FROM jsonb_to_recordset($jobs$[{"external_job_id":"R-0000187979","company_id":"rbc-capital-markets","company_name":"RBC Capital Markets","title":"Vice President, Global Investment Banking (Syndicated & Leveraged Finance)","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Investment Banking","specialization":"Leveraged Finance","seniority":"Vice President","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-16","application_deadline":"2026-10-14","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://rbc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RBCGLOBAL1/job/TORONTO-Ontario-Canada/Vice-President--Global-Investment-Banking--Syndicated---Leveraged-Finance---_R-0000187979-2/apply","source_url":"https://jobs.rbc.com/ca/en/job/RBCAA0088R0000187979EXTERNALENCA/Vice-President-Global-Investment-Banking-Syndicated-and-Leveraged-Finance","source_name":"RBC Capital Markets public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Vice President Investment Banking opportunity with RBC Capital Markets in Toronto, ON focused on Leveraged Finance.","description_text":"Job Description \n RBC Capital Markets is a part of the Royal Bank of Canada, one of the largest providers of financial services in the world with a purpose-driven, principles-led approach to delivering for our clients. RBC is a top ten bank globally and ranks among the top five banks in North America by market capitalization. In addition, RBC has one of the highest credit ratings of any financial institution globally.\n \n Our Investment Banking division is a top 10 Global Investment Bank which is well-established in the largest, most mature capital markets across North America, Europe, and the Asia Pacific Regions.\n \n Our Investment Banking division provides underwriting of equity and debt capital as well as strategic M&A advisory services for leading corporations, institutions, and governments throughout North America and around the world. We have built our successful investment banking business by focusing on our clients and the industry sectors in which they operate.\n \n What is the opportunity? \n \n RBC Capital Markets Global Investment Banking division is seeking a Vice President to join the Syndicated and Leveraged Finance (“SLF”) team in Toronto. The SLF team works collaboratively with colleagues across the Investment Bank in Canada, the U.S. and globally to support the financing of various types of transactions.\n \n This position is a unique opportunity to broaden your financial skillset, deepen your understanding of various credit markets and gain exposure to global capital markets.\n \n What will you do? \n - Lead financial analysis and due diligence in the context of originating, structuring, and executing credit related financing transactions (including LBOs)\n\n- Train, mentor, and supervise junior team members on day-to-day deliverables\n\n- Interpret credit market themes relevant to RBC’s corporate and financial sponsor clients and synthesize these for the benefit of a client or deal team\n\n- Take execution ownership of syndicated loan financings backing corporate M&A, LBOs, project financings, and general corporate purposes\n\n- Assist with preparation of pitch & advisory presentations, responses to RFPs, and other ad-hoc market research\n\n- Review and contribute to marketing materials and other documentation for credit related financing transactions including lender presentations\n\n- Collaborate with colleagues across corporate and investment banking coverage and product groups to deliver holistic financing solutions\n\n- Establish working relationships with bank investors and other market participants to gather market intelligence and optimize transaction execution\n\n \n What do you need to succeed? \n - Minimum 5 years of experience in investment banking, leveraged finance, private equity, equity research, corporate development, or accounting\n\n- Direct syndications experience leading transactions through the market considered a strong attribute\n\n- Experience structuring and/or leading bank market project financings is viewed as highly desirable\n\n- University degree, preferably in business/commerce, economics, “STEM” or other relevant disciplines\n\n- A desire to learn and a team-oriented mindset\n\n- Demonstrated superior track record in academic and professional endeavors\n\n- A clearly defined interest in investment banking and financial markets, and basic knowledge of market structure and themes\n\n- Strong computer skills, including high proficiency with Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint\n\n- Quantitative, analytical, and financial modeling skills\n\n- Adept written and verbal communication and data visualization skills\n\n- Ability to work well under pressure with multiple deadlines while maintaining careful attention to detail\n\n- Flexibility in schedule to meet client deadlines\n\n- Desire to develop a leadership skillset and make meaningful contributions in a fast-paced, team environment\n\n- CFA, CPA, P.Eng. or other relevant professional designations are considered an asset but not a requirement\n\n \n What’s in it for you? \n \n We thrive on the challenge to be our best, think progressively, continue our growth, and deliver trusted advice to help our clients thrive and communities prosper. We care about each other, reaching our individual / collective potential, making a difference to our communities, and achieving success that is mutual.\n \n From this opportunity you will gain:\n - A comprehensive Total Rewards Program including bonuses and flexible benefits, competitive compensation \n\n- Leaders who support your development through coaching and managing opportunities  \n\n- Opportunities to do challenging work \n\n- Flexible work/life balance options \n\n- Experience working in a dynamic, collaborative, and high-performing team at the #1 Investment Bank in Canada\n\n- Gain exposure and insight into the global capital markets\n\n- An in depth understanding of different credit markets, including the Bank Market, U.S. Term Loan B, and High Yield markets\n\n- Further development of fundamental investment banking skills such as financial modeling and analysis, transaction execution and negotiation, and in-depth industry and product knowledge\n\n- Work directly with senior levels of Canada's largest and fastest growing companies\n\n- Ability to make a difference through impactful transactions which help shape an industry\n\n- Peers who will help you develop a network and create long-term relationships\n\n- Leadership skills developed through coaching and mentoring junior team members\n\n- An appreciation for the importance of giving back your community as part of the many initiatives of RBC's Celebration of Impact\n\n- Future opportunities to work in other global offices\n\n \n \n **Application Process: \n \n Submit your cover letter, resume, and academic transcripts in one PDF document under the “resume” section of the online portal before the application deadline.   Please note that applications will be reviewed as they are received, and potential candidates may be contacted prior to the submission deadline.  Kindly address your application to the “Hiring Managers”.\n \n \n Job Skills \nInvestment Banking, Investment Operations, Investments Analysis, Long Term Planning, Order Processing, Quality Management, Recruiting, Risk Management, Trade Processing, Waterfall Model \n \n Additional Job Details \n Address: \n ROYAL BANK PLAZA, 200 BAY ST:TORONTO City: \n Toronto Country: \n Canada Work hours/week: \n 37.5 Employment Type: \n Full time Platform: \n CAPITAL MARKETS Job Type: \n Regular Pay Type: \n Salaried Posted Date: \n 2026-09-15 Application Deadline: \n 2026-10-14 Note : Applications will be accepted until 11:59 PM on the day prior to the application deadline date above \n \n \n Our Employment Opportunities \n \n At RBC, we are guided by living shared values of Client First, Integrity, Collaboration, Respect and Excellence and winning together as One RBC. We believe an inclusive workplace that has diverse perspectives is core to our continued growth as one of the largest and most successful banks in the world. Maintaining a workplace where our employees feel supported to perform at their best, effectively collaborate, drive innovation, and grow professionally helps to bring our Purpose to life and create value for our clients and communities. RBC strives to deliver this through policies and programs intended to foster a workplace based on respect, belonging and opportunity for all.\n \n \n Join our Talent Community \n\n Stay in-the-know about great career opportunities at RBC. Sign up and get customized info on our latest jobs, career tips and Recruitment events that matter to you. \n\n Expand your limits and create a new future together at RBC. Find out how we use our passion and drive to enhance the well-being of our clients and communities at jobs.rbc.com .","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"rbc:R-0000187979","data_quality_notes":"Role-specific Investment Banking evidence found in title.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"2619733","company_id":"cibc","company_name":"CIBC Capital Markets","title":"Analyst, Global Investment Banking","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Investment Banking","specialization":null,"seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-28","application_deadline":"2026-10-13","salary_min":105000,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/search/job/Toronto-ON/Analyst--Global-Investment-Banking_2619733","source_url":"https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/search/job/Toronto-ON/Analyst--Global-Investment-Banking_2619733","source_name":"CIBC Capital Markets public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Investment Banking opportunity with CIBC Capital Markets in Toronto, ON.","description_text":"We’re building a relationship-oriented bank for the modern world. We need talented, passionate professionals who are dedicated to doing what’s right for our clients. At CIBC, we embrace your strengths and your ambitions, so you are empowered at work. Our team members have what they need to make a meaningful impact and are truly valued for who they are and what they contribute. To learn more about CIBC, please visit CIBC.com What You’ll Be Doing CIBC Capital Markets provides corporate, government, and institutional clients with innovative solutions to help them raise capital, and grow and invest actively throughout North America, Latin America, and key financial centres around the world. Our mission is to bring Canadian Capital Markets products to Canada and the rest of the world, and also bring the world to Canada. CIBC Capital Markets Mergers & Acquisitions group of professionals are dedicated specifically to advising clients on mergers, acquisitions, joint ventures, hostile takeovers, buyouts, takeover defense and restructurings. There is an extensive amount of interaction with other groups within the firm in order to provide clients with customized financing and advisory solutions. As part of the M&A group, you will be expected to provide a broad range of analytical, research and presentation preparation support to all the professionals as well as gaining exposure to working with individuals from various groups across the firm. A team approach to executing coverage and financing assignments is designed to provide progressive, on-the-job training. The role of an Analyst within CIBC’s Mergers & Acquisitions (M&A) Investment Banking group is challenging and fast-paced. It requires dedication, a passion for excellence, and an exceptional work ethic. At CIBC we enable the work environment most optimal for you to thrive in your role. To successfully perform the work, you'll be on-site full-time. The expected annualized base salary for this role is $105,000. The base salary is determined by a variety of factors, including the candidate’s skills, experience, and job-related knowledge, as well as geographic location and specific business needs. Our compensation philosophy supports ongoing growth and development, enabling progression within the salary range as team members advance in their roles. In addition to base pay, compensation for this role includes participation in an annual discretionary incentive or bonus program. We are committed to providing fair, equitable, and competitive compensation opportunities for all employees and we encourage open conversations about compensation throughout the recruitment process. How You’ll Succeed Client Proposals - Assist in analyzing and developing proposals for mergers, asset or company divestitures or acquisitions, and other financial products and advisory services Transaction Execution – Take an active role in day-to-day transaction execution across sell-side, buy-side, fairness opinions, and other assignments Financial Modeling - Develop and audit sophisticated financial models Collaboration - Participate in cross-functional teams and liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in executing mandates or preparing proposals for clients Research - Prepare industry and financial analysis to determine client recommendations Analysis - Lead industry comparables and precedent transaction analyses Due Diligence - Assist in company due diligence investigations Marketing Materials - Prepare confidential offering memoranda and other marketing materials Relationship Building - Take advantage of in-depth technical and industry knowledge, as well as the geopolitical environment to generate ideas/opportunities that can be discussed with the relevant relationship manager and/or deal/coverage team. Coordinate client-focused and/or deal-focused “brainstorming” sessions with relevant team members and product specialists. Liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in preparing proposals for clients. Develop relationships and actively communicate with various appropriate contacts at the client. Develop and maintain an internal network with product groups, other business groups, etc. Develop and maintain an external network with the market (i.e. key stakeholders, prospects, etc.) and support CIBC’s image through involvement in community activities. Who You Are Previous Investment Banking or M&A transaction advisory experience required. Detailed, professional-level knowledge of Canadian M&A processes across different mandate types (sell-side, buy-side, etc.) is considered an asset. You have completed an undergraduate degree in Finance or Engineering. Completion of a CPA or CFA, is beneficial. You know that details matter. Extremely dedicated and motivated individual with high career aspirations. Must be capable of assuming high levels of responsibility within short time frames. Ability to work well under pressure with multiple or competing deadlines while maintaining meticulous attention to detail. Must be able to accept flexibility in required personal time commitments to complete work assignments. You can demonstrate technical skills (Programs, Methodologies, Systems). Excellent analytical abilities, including demonstrated knowledge of valuation techniques and practices. Knowledge of accounting principles relating to financial statement preparation and business combinations. Strong technical skills as it relates to Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint), industry technology (Bloomberg, Factset) and applicable software. You have advanced internal and client-focused communication skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills are important to ensuring smooth transaction execution and timely delivery of materials. Ability to comfortably liaise with equivalent professionals on the client side is considered a strong asset. You’re motivated by collective success. Well-developed interpersonal and relationship-building skills in order to develop, manage and leverage relationships with clients, and internal and/or external business partners. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills sufficient to provide detailed explanation and interpretation of factual and conceptual information and ideas related to complex technical and conceptual issues. Unquestioned professionalism, ethics and reputation and proven ability to exercise strong independent judgment when making business decisions and/or representing CIBC Capital Markets. #LI-TA What CIBC Offers At CIBC, your goals are a priority. We start with your strengths and ambitions as an employee and strive to create opportunities to tap into your potential. We aspire to give you a career, rather than just a paycheck. We work to recognize you in meaningful, personalized ways including a competitive salary, incentive pay, banking benefits, a benefits program*, defined benefit pension plan*, an employee share purchase plan, a vacation offering, wellbeing support, and MomentMakers, our social, points-based recognition program. Our spaces and technological toolkit will make it simple to bring together great minds to create innovative solutions that make a difference for our clients. We cultivate a culture where you can express your ambition through initiatives like Purpose Day; a paid day off dedicated for you to use to invest in your growth and development. *Subject to plan and program terms and conditions What you need to know CIBC is committed to creating an inclusive environment where all team members and clients feel like they belong. We seek applicants with a wide range of abilities and we provide an accessible candidate experience. If you need accommodation, please contact Mailbox.careers-carrieres@cibc.com CIBC is committed to clarity in our hiring process. All roles posted are opportunities we’re actively recruiting for, unless stated otherwise. You need to be legally eligible to work at the location(s) specified above and, where applicable, must have a valid work or study permit. We may ask you to complete an attribute-based assessment and other skills test (such as simulation, coding, French proficiency). We use artificial intelligence tools during the recruitment process. Our goal for the application process is to get to know more about you, all that you have to offer, and give you the opportunity to learn more about us. Job Location Toronto-161 Bay St., 6th Employment Type Regular Weekly Hours 37.5 Skills Analytical Thinking, Capital Markets, Financial Markets Analysis, Investment Banking, Investment Valuation, Mergers and Acquisitions (M&A), Research Analysis, Wealth Management, Work Collaboratively","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"cibc:2619733","data_quality_notes":"Role-specific Investment Banking evidence found in title.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"2619741","company_id":"cibc","company_name":"CIBC Capital Markets","title":"Associate, Global Investment Banking","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Investment Banking","specialization":null,"seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-28","application_deadline":"2026-10-13","salary_min":135000,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://cibc.wd3.m