rt to all the professionals within the group. Associates are assigned to a variety of transactions and advisory projects, such as mergers & acquisitions, brokerage transactions, divestitures, equity and debt financings, and strategic advisory projects. As part of the Investment Banking group, you will gain exposure to working with individuals from various groups across the firm globally. A team approach to executing coverage and financing assignments is designed to provide progressive, on-the-job training At CIBC we enable the work environment most optimal for you to thrive in your role. To successfully perform the work, you'll be on-site full-time. The expected annualized base salary for this role is $135,000. The base salary is determined by a variety of factors, including the candidate’s skills, experience, and job-related knowledge, as well as geographic location and specific business needs. Our compensation philosophy supports ongoing growth and development, enabling progression within the salary range as team members advance in their roles. In addition to base pay, compensation for this role includes participation in an annual discretionary incentive or bonus program. We are committed to providing fair, equitable, and competitive compensation opportunities for all employees and we encourage open conversations about compensation throughout the recruitment process. How you'll succeed Client Engagement – Play an active role in the execution of client mandate. Conduct deal related due diligence activities and present findings internally. Participate in developing investor presentation materials and in “road show” marketing activities. Work with outside working group members including legal advisors, accounting advisors, auditors, etc. Responsible for the overall information and communication flow on deal teams Relationship Building – Take advantage of in-depth technical and industry knowledge, as well as the geopolitical environment to generate ideas/opportunities that can be discussed with the relevant relationship manager and/or deal/coverage team. You will coordinate client-focused and/or deal-focused “brainstorming” sessions with relevant team members and product specialists. Liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in preparing proposals for clients. Develop relationships and actively communicate with various appropriate contacts at the client. Develop and maintain an internal network with product groups, other business groups, etc. Develop and maintain an external network with the market (i.e., key stakeholders, prospects, etc.) and support CIBC’s image through involvement in community activities. Teamwork – Partner with your team to connect clients with opportunities. Participate in cross-functional teams and liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in executing mandates or preparing proposals for clients. Well-developed interpersonal and relationship building skills to develop, manage and leverage relationships with clients, and internal and/or external business partners. Unquestioned professionalism, ethics and reputation and established ability to exercise strong independent judgment when making business decisions and/or representing CIBC Capital Markets Who you are You can demonstrate 3-5 years of experience in real estate, investment banking, corporate finance, and/or private equity. CA, CPA, or CFA designations are an asset. It is preferred if you have detailed professional level knowledge of the Canadian real estate sector. You're digitally savvy. You have excellent analytical abilities, including demonstrated knowledge of valuation techniques and practices. Knowledge of accounting principles relating to financial statement preparation and business combinations. Strong technical skills as it relates to Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint), industry technology (Bloomberg & FactSet) and applicable software. Experience with Argus Enterprise is strongly preferred. You’re passionate about people. You have well-developed written and verbal communication skills sufficient to provide detailed explanation and interpretation of factual and conceptual information and ideas related to technical and conceptual issues. You know that details matter. You are an extremely dedicated and motivated individual with high career aspirations. Must be capable of assuming important levels of responsibility within brief time frames What CIBC Offers At CIBC, your goals are a priority. We start with your strengths and ambitions as an employee and strive to create opportunities to tap into your potential. We aspire to give you a career, rather than just a paycheck. We work to recognize you in meaningful, personalized ways including a competitive salary, incentive pay, banking benefits, a benefits program*, defined benefit pension plan*, an employee share purchase plan, a vacation offering, wellbeing support, and MomentMakers, our social, points-based recognition program. Our spaces and technological toolkit will make it simple to bring together great minds to create innovative solutions that make a difference for our clients. We cultivate a culture where you can express your ambition through initiatives like Purpose Day; a paid day off dedicated for you to use to invest in your growth and development. *Subject to plan and program terms and conditions What you need to know CIBC is committed to creating an inclusive environment where all team members and clients feel like they belong. We seek applicants with a wide range of abilities and we provide an accessible candidate experience. If you need accommodation, please contact Mailbox.careers-carrieres@cibc.com CIBC is committed to clarity in our hiring process. All roles posted are opportunities we’re actively recruiting for, unless stated otherwise. You need to be legally eligible to work at the location(s) specified above and, where applicable, must have a valid work or study permit. We may ask you to complete an attribute-based assessment and other skills test (such as simulation, coding, French proficiency). We use artificial intelligence tools during the recruitment process. Our goal for the application process is to get to know more about you, all that you have to offer, and give you the opportunity to learn more about us. Job Location Toronto-161 Bay St., 6th Employment Type Regular Weekly Hours 37.5 Skills Advisory Services, Analytical Thinking, Customer Experience (CX), Financial Modeling, Financial Research, High Net Worth Individuals, Investment Banking, Investment Valuation, Private Equity, Wealth Management","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"cibc:2619741","data_quality_notes":"Role-specific Investment Banking evidence found in title.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"url-4f36e26ae19ef78c45e7","company_id":"agentis","company_name":"Agentis Capital","title":"Managing Director - Infrastructure M&A Advisory","location_display":"Toronto, ON / Vancouver, BC","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Investment Banking","specialization":"Mergers & Acquisitions","seniority":"Managing Director","employment_type":null,"program_type":null,"term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":null,"application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/Agentis-Capital-Advisors/b238f4bb-03fd-4956-b5dd-7f1dec4b2ad6","source_url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/Agentis-Capital-Advisors/b238f4bb-03fd-4956-b5dd-7f1dec4b2ad6","source_name":"Agentis Capital public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Managing Director Investment Banking opportunity with Agentis Capital in Toronto, ON / Vancouver, BC focused on Mergers & Acquisitions.","description_text":"Managing Director - Infrastructure 