t--Natural-Resources-Investments_R4631","source_url":"https://investpsp.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/psp_careers/job/Montreal/Analyst---Senior-Analyst--Natural-Resources-Investments_R4631","source_name":"PSP Investments public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Institutional Investing opportunity with PSP Investments in Montreal, QC focused on Natural Resources.","description_text":"ABOUT US We’re one of Canada’s largest pension investors, with CAD$299.7 billion of net assets as of March 31, 2025. We invest funds for the pension plans of the federal public service, the Canadian Forces, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Reserve Force. Headquartered in Ottawa, PSP Investments has its principal business office in Montréal and offices in New York, London and Hong Kong. Capturing and leading complex global investments requires us to work as one to seize valuable opportunities, in close collaboration with some of the world’s top companies. At PSP Investments, you’ll join a team of motivated and engaged professionals, dedicated to propelling our organization further than ever before. ABOUT YOUR ROLE As an Analyst/ Senior Analyst, Natural Resources Investments, you’ll: Perform investment analysis and execute transactions Perform preliminary analysis of investment opportunities, meet with prospective partners and industry experts and prepare summary reports Perform in-depth due diligence of potential investments, identify key investment merits and risks, meet with management teams, review documentation and work in conjunction with partners and third-party consultants Build detailed financial models, including performing extensive sensitivity analyses, review of financial projections and valuation assumptions Participate in the preparation of investment recommendation memorandums for investment approval Participate in presentations to various committees as required Represent the NR Team across the Timber, Agriculture and Investment Industries Active networking with industry experts, consultants, peers and industry players Attend conferences, organize meetings and keep up to date on industry trends Participate in building deal-flow and becoming a subject matter expert Actively Manage Investments Monitor financial and operating results Interact with management and operating partners Work alongside management teams of portfolio companies on specific projects to create value Note: This position requires travel. WHAT YOU’LL NEED University degree with strong academic standing Two (2) to four (4) years of professional experience in private investments, investment banking, corporate finance, or in a natural resources company considered a strong asset Professional designation: CFA an asset Superior level of proficiency with business software and analytical tools Strong financial skills, including experience in building financial models, and familiar with financial statements Project management skills and ability to meet tight deadlines Mature, driven, motivated and ability to take initiative Responsible, diligent, and able to work independently and as part of a team Good attention to detail and presentation of information Good communications skills in either Spanish or Portuguese is essential to be successful in this position. Good communications skills in English and French (or willingness to learn) regular interactions in English with investment partners based outside of Quebec Example: peers, bankers, brokerage firms, etc. and PSP employees in our offices in Hong Kong, London and New York, and interactions in French with employees in our local offices in Montreal and Ottawa We offer a tailored employee experience and competitive total rewards and benefits package* designed to attract and retain global diverse talent, reward performance, and reinforce business strategies and priorities. Beyond salary and incentive pay eligibility, you have access to: Investment in career development Comprehensive group insurance plans Competitive pension plans Unlimited access to virtual healthcare services and wellness programs Gender-inclusive paid family leave policy : up to 26 weeks for primary caregivers, 5 weeks for secondary caregivers A personalized family-building support , from pre-pregnancy to menopause, with available financial assistance Vacation days available on day one with additional days on milestone service anniversaries, and summer Friday afternoons off A hybrid work model with a mix of in-office and remote days *Benefits package may vary based on your employee type. At PSP Investments , we aim to provide a workplace where everyone feels valued, safe, respected and empowered to grow. As part of this leadership commitment, we strongly encourage applications from all qualified applicants and strive to offer an inclusive and accessible candidate experience. If you require any accommodation for any part of the recruitment process, please let us know. Visit us on www.investpsp.com/en/ Follow us on LinkedIn #LI-GR1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"psp-investments:R4631","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100915","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"New Grad Analyst, Investment Management Rotational Program (Fundamental and Quantitative Roles)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"New Graduate Program","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-09","application_deadline":"2026-10-07","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/New-Grad-Analyst--Investment-Management-Rotational-Program--Fundamental-and-Quantitative-Roles-_JR100915","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/New-Grad-Analyst--Investment-Management-Rotational-Program--Fundamental-and-Quantitative-Roles-_JR100915","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"New Graduate Program Analyst Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 7, 2026 Opportunity Opportunity Are you ready to kickstart your career with hands-on experience at a global multi-asset class institutional investment manager? If you're passionate about financial markets or economics and want to make a meaningful impact in your community, AIMCo's rotational program is the perfect opportunity for you. We are accepting recent or upcoming new graduates into the 18-month rotational program with a start date in May 2027. Throughout the term, you’ll rotate through three asset classes and get the opportunity to work on special projects, while gaining valuable experience within the Investment Management space. You’ll get a chance to complete three 6-month rotations and gain a unique perspective and deep understanding of our Investment Management function, which is comprised of the following asset classes: Public Equities, Fixed Income, Private Debt & Loan, Mortgages, Infrastructure & Renewable Resources, Real Estate, Private Equity, and Multi-Asset Portfolio Management. We are looking for several individuals to join in either fundamental investment focused or quantitative focused roles. Successful candidate will be intellectually curious, adaptable, and collaborative individuals who are eager to learn and contribute in a fast-paced environment. At AIMCo, you'll work alongside experienced investment professionals while developing technical, analytical, and communication skills that will accelerate your career. This opportunity is open to candidates who are willing to relocate to Calgary, Alberta, and we encourage all interested individuals to apply! What You’ ll Do: Daily tasks and projects will differ from team to team but overall, the New Grad Analyst can expect to be involved in: Fundamental Focused: Evaluate and support the execution of investment opportunities across public and private markets, including direct, co-investment, and fund investments. Conduct research and analysis on companies, industries, funds, and market trends to inform investment decisions. Build financial models, valuations, and investment underwriting analyses. Assess opportunities through financial statement analysis, market research, and due diligence on business models, competitive positioning, management teams, risks, and value creation potential. Prepare investment research reports and present recommendations to the investment team. Monitor portfolio holdings, market developments, and emerging investment opportunities and risks. Collaborate with investment teams on idea generation, transaction execution, portfolio management, and asset monitoring. Leverage investment research platforms (e.g., Bloomberg, FactSet, Capital IQ) and AI-enabled tools to enhance research, analysis, reporting, and operational efficiency . Demonstrate proficiency in AI-assisted analytical workflows and maintain awareness of emerging technologies relevant to investment management. Quantitative Focused: Develop and enhance analytical tools, automated workflows, and investment data infrastructure. Build and improve fi nancial models , quantitativ e models, databases, and analytical frameworks to support investment decision-making. Conduct quantitative research and data analysis across markets, asset classes, and risk factors to generate investment insights. Support portfolio managers and traders with risk analytics, performance attribution, portfolio construction, and investment recommendations. Backtest investment strategies and monitor model performance. Evaluate and implement new technologies , data sources, and analytical techniques. Collaborate with investment teams on research, portfolio management, and investment projects. Prepare presentations, reports, and data visualizations to communicate research findings and recommendations. Leverage AI-enabled tools and emerging technologies to enhance research, analytics, reporting, and operational efficiency. Ideal Candidate Qualifications Fundamental Focused : Recent undergraduate or master's graduate in Business, Finance, Economics, Accounting, or a related field (completed within the last 12 months). Previous internship or work experience in investment banking, private equity, asset management, or a related field. Solid understanding of valuation and investment analysis techniques, including discounted cash flow (DCF), leveraged buyout (LBO), and other relevant methodologies. Proficiency in financial modeling and the ability to translate quantitative and qualitative information into investment insights. Advanced skills in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint. Strong critical-thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills with a high attention to detail. Proven ability to synthesize quantitative and qualitative information into well-supported investment insights and recommendations. Self-motivated, intellectually curious, and able to thrive in a fast-paced environment while managing multiple priorities. Demonstrated interest in investing, capital markets, and long-term value creation. Progress toward or completion of the CFA designation is an asset. Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo's values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity, and collabora tion. Quantitative Focused: Recent undergraduate, master's, or PhD graduate in a quantitative discipline such as Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Engineering, Economics, Finance, Physics, or Data Science (completed within the last 12 months). Experience working with large datasets and conducting quantitative analysis using Python through internships, academic research, or related experience. Strong programming skills in Python (e.g., pandas, NumPy, SciPy); experience with SQL, VBA, or other programming languages is an asset. Knowledge of statistics, econometrics, machine learning, optimization, and quantitative modeling techniques. Ability to translate quantitative and qualitative analysis into actionable insights and recommendations. Strong analytical, critical-thinking, problem-solving, and communication skills, with a high degree of attention to detail. Advanced Excel skills, including data analysis, financial modeling, and automation. Experience conducting financial, economic, or quantitative research; familiarity with Bloomberg, Capital IQ, FactSet, or similar platforms is an asset. Exposure to areas such as quantitative investing, machine learning, data visualization, portfolio construction, risk modeling, actuarial science, CFA studies, or academic research is preferred. Self-motivated, intellectually curious, and able to work independently while collaborating effectively in a team environment. Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo's values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity, and collabora tion. Success Measures Success at the end of your 1 8 -month term will be determined by the undertaking and completion of specified daily tasks while collaborating alongside the team, sharing your ideas, contributing to several ongoing projects, and assisting the department with implementing and improving process efficiencies. There is potential for extension and/or full-time employment once rotation is complete. ** NOTE this role will close at 11:59 PM MST on October 6 , 202 7 . Application instructions : Please include your resume, university transcript(s) and cover letter in your application. Recruitment Timeline: What to Expect Student s can expect the followin g recruitment timelines. September 8: Job Posting Opens October 6: Application deadline ( job posting will close at 11:59pm MST) Mid-October: I nitial Candidate Outreach Selected candidates will be contacted to participate in the pre-screening process End of October : Interviews Begin Selected candidates can expect two rounds of interviews. Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100915","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility. Career-path classification depends on metadata or description text.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100908","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, External Partnerships, Public Equities (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Public Equities","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-03","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--External-Partnerships--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100908","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--External-Partnerships--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100908","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Public Equities.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity AIMCo’s Public Equities team provides core asset class exposure to Canadian and global equity markets. The team combines internally and externally managed strategies to help meet our clients’ objectives. Internally managed investments include Systematic, Alpha, and Fundamental strategies that currently invest in more than 45 countries around the world. Externally-managed investments include long-only equity and hedge fund strategies and are employed in areas where internal management does not offer a competitive or cost advantage. Within Public Equities, the External Partnerships team performs due diligence on, monitors and manages a wide range of hedge fund and Equity strategies on behalf of clients. The team is seeking an intern for Summer 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026 Responsibilities: Assisting in the development of reports and tools to help portfolio managers increase the efficiency and transparency of our products Assisting the team to more accurately assess and monitor externally-managed investments Assisting in the research and development of quantitative models in order to perform portfolio construction on our products Collaborating with team members to develop a practical understanding of the day-to-day operations of a global investment firm Our Ideal Candidate Qualifications: In pursuit of an undergraduate or graduate degree in finance, economics, math, statistics, computer science or related field Demonstrated interest in and knowledge of investment management through involvement in related extra-curricular activities Pursuit of, or the intent to pursue, the CFA designation is an asset Exposure to Bloomberg or Capital IQ is an asset Experience with programming, especially in Python, is an asset Collaborative team player with good communication and relationship building skills High attention to detail and a desire to advance analytical skillsets Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others Success Measures: Success at the end of your term will be determined by your ability to seek out learning opportunities and become involved in multiple projects, tasks, responsibilities and investments. You will have developed an increased understanding of investment concepts and market knowledge, and a new appreciation of finance and investment management. A student who goes above and beyond expectations will participate in multiple projects and add value to team initiatives. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100908","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100900","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, Economics & Investment Research (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Economics---Investment-Research--May-2027-_JR100900","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Economics---Investment-Research--May-2027-_JR100900","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity Do you have passion for the financial markets, the desire to work closely in support of client investment goals, and the ability to think outside the box? We are seeking a talented Summer Student to join the Economics & Investment Research function who can deliver best-in-class applied quantitative economic and investment research and corresponding tools. This team builds a house view on the economic outlook, provides country macroeconomic research and currency views to the investment teams alongside macroeconomic scenario analysis for client asset allocation and total portfolio risk. It is also responsible for the research needs for AIMCO’s Investment Strategy and Investment teams on top-down strategic and tactical research initiatives across client portfolios and asset classes. Note: This is a full-time, 4-month term starting in May 2027 through August 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Conduct research based on macroeconomic and financial data analysis in support of client advice and total portfolio management Assisting in gathering data and statistical modelling of investment research projects Working collaboratively with departments such as Multi-Asset Portfolio Management, Risk Management, Client Investment Strategy, and various investment teams to provide effective debate to findings and to explore creative solutions to unique portfolio management challenges Preparing written materials and presentations for the effective delivery and communication of investment research to clients, investment teams and to provide education and transparency into the Economics & Investment Research function Participate in the team’s focus on building LLM-based prompting strategies, pipelines and agentic workflows Ideal Candidate Qualifications: Currently enrolled in a bachelor’s, master’s degree or PhD in a quantitative field (Mathematics, Economics, Actuarial Science, Finance, Engineering, Computer Science or related) Experience with software programming language (R or Python) and proficiency with Microsoft Applications (Excel, Word, Outlook) is required Experience with building LLM-based processes and infrastructure is an asset Knowledge of statistical/econometrics and optimization methods is an asset Exceptional attention to detail, and an ability to manage multiple tasks and work under pressure to meet deadlines Effective analytical, organization, time management and communication skills Investment management or finance exposure would be considered an asset Demonstrates a commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others Success Measures: You will have taken a hands-on, key support role in providing macro and investment research insights to key stakeholders across our clients and the organization. You will have also developed a deep understanding of AIMCo’s client structure and client investment strategies and build collaborative relationships through cross-functional teams. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100900","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility. Career-path classification depends on metadata or description text.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100896","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, Alpha Strategies, Public Equities (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Alpha-Strategies--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100896","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Alpha-Strategies--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100896","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity The Alpha Strategies team operates as part of the Public Equities team at AIMCo managing a variety of market neutral relative value and arbitrage strategies using a combination of fundamental and quantitative analysis. We are actively engaged in capital markets and invest in equity and equity-linked opportunities across our strategies. This role will strengthen the team and investment strategy by providing support with investment research, portfolio analytics, operational and data management and technology infrastructure projects. Note: This is a 4-month, full-time term from May 2027 through August 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Contributing to the day-to-day operational support and management of the Alpha Strategies portfolio Contributing to idea generation and investment research Conduct fundamental equity and credit research Build and maintain valuation models, screening databases and related data sets Proactively developing and communicating research for the team Collaborating with a variety of teams within AIMCo to achieve common goals Our Ideal Candidate: In pursuit of an undergraduate degree in finance, economics, math, statistics, computer science or related field. Proven financial modelling skills and ability to conduct detailed financial analysis. Strong technical skills (Bloomberg, Capital IQ, Factset, Excel, Word, PowerPoint, etc.). Working towards the completion of CFA Charter or other related designation is an asset. Programming/data analysis skills and prior trading experience are considered assets. Team player with strong communication and relationship building skills. Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrates a commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others. Success Measures: Success at the end of your term will be determined by your ability to seek out learning opportunities and become involved in multiple projects, tasks, responsibilities, and investments. You will have developed an increased understanding of investment concepts and market knowledge, and a new appreciation of finance and investment management. A student who goes above and beyond expectations will participate in multiple projects and add value to team initiatives. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100896","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100895","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, Public Equities (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Public Equities","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100895","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Public-Equities--May-2027-_JR100895","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Public Equities.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity AIMCo’s Public Equities team provides core asset class exposure to Canadian and global equity markets. The team combines internally and externally managed strategies to help meet our clients’ objectives. Internally managed investments include Systematic, Alpha, and Fundamental strategies that currently invest in more than 45 countries around the world. Externally-managed investments include long-only equity and hedge fund strategies and are employed in areas where internal management does not offer a competitive or cost advantage. Within Public Equities, the Portfolio Construction team helps bring these strategies together, along with other types of strategies, to offer performant products to clients within our risk tolerance at competitive costs. The Beta Management team manages the asset class’s index exposures. Each of these teams is seeking an intern for Summer 2027. Note: This is a 4-month, full-time term from May 2027 through August 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Assisting in the development of reports and tools to help portfolio managers increase the efficiency and transparency of our products Assisting the team to more accurately assess product positioning across different country, industry, and style factors, for the purposes of considering new or existing investment opportunities Assisting in the research and development of quantitative models and alpha signals Collaborating with team members to develop a practical understanding of the day-to-day operations of a global investment firm Our Ideal Candidate: In pursuit of an undergraduate or graduate degree in finance, economics, math, statistics, computer science or related field Demonstrated interest in and knowledge of investment management through involvement in related extra-curricular activities Pursuit of, or the intent to pursue, the CFA designation is an asset Exposure to Bloomberg or Capital IQ is an asset Experience with programming, especially in Python, is an asset Collaborative team player with good communication and relationship building skills High attention to detail and a desire to advance analytical skillsets Success Measures: Success at the end of your term will be determined by your ability to seek out learning opportunities and become involved in multiple projects, tasks, responsibilities and investments. You will have developed an increased understanding of investment concepts and market knowledge, and a new appreciation of finance and investment management. A student who goes above and beyond expectations will participate in multiple projects and add value to team initiatives. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100895","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100893","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, Private Equity (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Private Equity","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Private-Equity--May-2027-_JR100893","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Private-Equity--May-2027-_JR100893","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Private Equity opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Private Equity.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity The Student, Private Equity at AIMCo is a unique role where you’ll gain experience analyzing Private Equity investments alongside an experienced and focused team of investment professionals, while contributing to the financial security of hundreds of thousands of Albertans. In this role you will gain experience analyzing Private Equity investment opportunities across a diverse range of industries. In addition, you will have the opportunity to continue to build AIMCo’s Private Equity portfolio collaboratively and help manage existing assets under the guidance of dedicated investment professionals. Through these activities you will learn a number of new skills, such as the evaluation of Private Equity investments and funds, financial analysis, and valuation. Note: This is a 4-month, full-time term from May 2027 through August 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Participate in the identification and evaluation of new investment opportunities, including direct investments, secondaries, and funds Conduct research and analysis on a broad array of industries, sectors, funds, or other opportunities identified by Private Equity professionals Maintain and update portfolio company and fund investment materials and track investment performance Participate in interactions with global Private Equity fund managers and summarize key takeaways on internal databases Work with other investment professionals to support ongoing daily activities Our Ideal Candidate: Completion of second- or third-year undergraduate studies in Finance, Commerce, Business Administration, Accounting, or other related fields. Demonstrated interest in investing and analyzing businesses in various industries Excellent knowledge of finance, accounting, and economic concepts Strong research, analytical, quantitative and problem-solving abilities Excellent written, interpersonal, and presentation skills Exceptional attention to detail and strong work ethic Ability to manage multiple tasks and work under pressure to meet deadlines Builds strong relationships with team members including celebrating team accomplishments Proven track record of outstanding academic achievement and performance High proficiency with Microsoft Applications (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook) Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others Success Measures: AIMCo’s most successful students are team oriented, intellectually curious, exhibit a passion for finance and investing, and are results-oriented with exceptional finance and communications skills. Students with a high degree of professionalism can expect to be exposed to meetings and calls with other internal and external parties, such as management teams, other private equity investors, investment bankers, consultants and lawyers. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100893","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR102500","company_id":"hoopp","company_name":"HOOPP","title":"Associate, Cross-Asset Thematic Investing","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Public Equities","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-01","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":98000,"salary_max":148000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Associate--Cross-Asset-Thematic-Investing_JR102500","source_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Associate--Cross-Asset-Thematic-Investing_JR102500","source_name":"HOOPP public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Institutional Investing opportunity with HOOPP in Toronto, ON focused on Public Equities.","description_text":"Why you’ll love working here: high-performance, people-focused culture our commitment that equity, diversity, and inclusion are fundamental to our work environment and business success, which helps employees feel valued and empowered to be their authentic selves learning and development initiatives, including workshops, Speaker Series events and access to LinkedIn Learning, that support employees’ career growth membership in HOOPP’s world class defined benefit pension plan, which can serve as an important part of your retirement security competitive, 100% company-paid extended health and dental benefits for permanent employees, including coverage supporting our team's diversity and mental health (e.g., gender affirmation, fertility and drug treatment, psychological support benefits of $2,500 per year, parental leave top-up, and a health spending account). optional post-retirement health and dental benefits subsidized at 50% yoga classes, meditation workshops, nutritional consultations, and wellness seminars the opportunity to make a difference and help take care of those who care for us, by providing a financially secure retirement for Ontario healthcare workers Job Summary Reporting to the Senior Portfolio Manager, Cross-Asset Thematic Investing, the Associate will be a core member of a small investment team managing thematic investment portfolios across global public equities, rates, credit, currencies and commodities. The Associate will contribute across the investment process — from identifying cross-market themes, policy shifts, market trends and dislocations to building investment conviction and determining the most effective expression of those views across markets and instruments. To support this process, the Associate will build and apply AI-enabled research workflows to evaluate market developments, synthesize diverse data and perspectives, deepen research and build conviction around the most promising ideas, test investment theses against a wide range of evidence, and assess how potential trades fit within the broader portfolio. Success in the role requires strong investment judgment and demonstrated proficiency in developing, validating and integrating these workflows into investment decision-making. What you will do: Proactively identify and evaluate investment opportunities arising from macroeconomic developments, structural themes, policy changes, industry dynamics, market positioning and dislocations across global markets. Develop investment theses by defining the underlying causal logic, economic and market transmission mechanisms, key drivers, catalysts, scenarios, expected payoff, principal risks, monitoring indicators and developments that may challenge the thesis. Conduct flexible yet structured fundamental research at the level required by each opportunity. Assignments may range from analyzing a security, market segment or industry to evaluating a country, policy development, broader market trend or cross-asset dynamic. This may include modelling market regimes or developing relative-value frameworks. Design and maintain AI-enabled investment research workflows that support market screening, hypothesis generation, research, and portfolio construction. Specifically, the Associate will use AI-assisted coding and approved AI tools to accelerate document analysis, data extraction and management, information synthesis, financial and economic model development, and ongoing thesis monitoring. Translate research into investable expressions by comparing individual securities, baskets, relative-value trades and derivatives, including option structures. Assess implementation alternatives based on expected return, asymmetry, carry, liquidity, timing, catalysts, downside risk, implementation complexity and fit within the broader portfolio. Monitor portfolio positions and investment ideas by tracking performance, exposures, risks, catalysts, thesis indicators and relevant market developments. Support portfolio management activities, including position sizing, portfolio construction, performance tracking and adherence to investment guidelines and risk budgets. Undertake ad hoc investment research on macroeconomic and cross-asset themes that may support the team or broader investment activities across HOOPP. Coordinate with internal stakeholders, including investment, operations, legal, risk and other teams, to support the execution and ongoing management of investment activities. Communicate conclusions and recommended actions clearly, using the format best suited to the investment decision, including discussions, models, dashboards, concise research notes and presentations. What you bring: Completion of a university degree in Finance, Economics, Business Administration, Mathematics, Statistics, Engineering, Data Science, or another relevant discipline. Interdisciplinary or dual-degree backgrounds are welcome, as are candidates who have developed a comparable combination of investment, analytical and technical capabilities through their professional experience. 2 to 5 years of relevant experience on a global macro or thematic investment team, or in another public-markets role involving investment research, cross-market analysis, idea generation and portfolio decision-making. Experience translating macroeconomic, policy and industry developments into actionable ideas across asset classes is preferred. Strong organizational skills and a structured approach to investment decision-making, combined with the judgment and adaptability to operate effectively in a fluid environment and balance multiple, changing priorities. A high degree of initiative and ownership, demonstrated through a proactive approach to driving work forward, together with a strong interest in cross-asset investing. Excellent investment research skills, including the ability to frame a question, develop a testable thesis, identify the most important drivers and catalysts, distinguish signal from noise and revise conclusions when the evidence changes. Strong quantitative capabilities and practical knowledge of statistics, econometrics, time-series analysis or applied machine-learning methods. Proficiency in Python and Excel. Demonstrated proficiency in applying AI tools in research and workflow development. Strong judgment, intellectual curiosity and attention to detail, with the ability to maintain analytical rigour under time pressure. Strong oral and written communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in a collaborative team environment. A high degree of professionalism, integrity and accountability. Completion of, or progress toward, a professional designation such as the CFA is considered an asset. Relevant graduate-level technical or quantitative training may also be beneficial. The expected annual base salary range for this role is: $98,000 - $148,000 CAD The actual base salary offered to the successful candidate may vary based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, individual's expertise and level of experience applicable to the role they are being offered. This role is eligible to participate in discretionary incentive plan(s), subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable incentive plan text. This job posting is for a newly created role. HOOPP may use artificial intelligence tools to assist in screening, assessing and selecting applicants for this position. These tools support our recruitment process but do not replace human judgment and decision-making.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"hoopp:JR102500","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility. Career-path classification depends on metadata or description text.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR102445","company_id":"hoopp","company_name":"HOOPP","title":"Associate, Private Equity (18-month contract)","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Contract","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-06-19","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":98000,"salary_max":148000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Associate--Private-Equity--18-month-contract-_JR102445","source_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Associate--Private-Equity--18-month-contract-_JR102445","source_name":"HOOPP public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Contract Associate Private Equity opportunity with HOOPP in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"Why you’ll love working here: high-performance, people-focused culture our commitment that equity, diversity, and inclusion are fundamental to our work environment and business success, which helps employees feel valued and empowered to be their authentic selves learning and development initiatives, including workshops, Speaker Series events and access to LinkedIn Learning, that support employees’ career growth membership in HOOPP’s world class defined benefit pension plan, which can serve as an important part of your retirement security competitive, 100% company-paid extended health and dental benefits for permanent employees, including coverage supporting our team's diversity and mental health (e.g., gender affirmation, fertility and drug treatment, psychological support benefits of $2,500 per year, parental leave top-up, and a health spending account). optional post-retirement health and dental benefits subsidized at 50% yoga classes, meditation workshops, nutritional consultations, and wellness seminars the opportunity to make a difference and help take care of those who care for us, by providing a financially secure retirement for Ontario healthcare workers The Healthcare of Ontario Pension Plan (HOOPP) is one of the top-performing and fastest-growing pension funds in the world, with $131.9 billion in net assets under management globally. HOOPP invests in all major asset classes, including fixed income, public equity, credit, private equity, real estate, and infrastructure, and is headquartered in Toronto, Canada. At HOOPP, we are committed to providing secure retirement income to over 504,000 Ontario healthcare workers, while maintaining a high-performance culture of integrity, collaboration, and continuous learning. HOOPP Capital Partners (“HCP”) is the private equity arm of the Healthcare of Ontario Pension Plan (HOOPP), managing over $20 billion in assets. Our team executes investments globally across direct, co-investment, and fund strategies, with a portfolio that includes direct investments companies like Chobani, Taylor Guitars, and Herschel Supply Co. Job Summary As an Associate on the HCP team, you will gain hands-on exposure to the full investment lifecycle—including sourcing, evaluating, executing, and monitoring private equity investments. This is a foundational role designed for intellectually curious, motivated individuals eager to contribute to a lean, collaborative team and grow within private markets investing. You will work closely with senior investment professionals, playing a meaningful role in both investment execution and portfolio management. The role offers strong development opportunities with increasing responsibility based on performance. What you will do Investment Execution Support due diligence on potential direct investment, co-investment and fund opportunities Build and maintain dynamic and user-friendly financial models for valuation and return analysis Prepare and contribute to investment memos and committee materials Conduct industry, company, and market research to inform investment theses Assist in evaluating deal structuring options, terms, and implications Portfolio Management Monitor financial and operational performance of portfolio companies and fund investments Assist with periodic valuations, performance attribution, and reporting on existing investments Investigate and model financing alternatives or follow-on investment opportunities Strategic and Internal Initiatives Contribute to research and analysis on investment themes, sectors, and structures Support internal strategic initiatives including process improvements and knowledge sharing Engage with internal stakeholders across legal, tax, and operations to support deal execution What You Bring 2-4 years of experience in investment banking or private equity University degree in Finance, Commerce, Economics, Engineering, or a quantitative field with strong academic performance Demonstrated strong skills in financial modeling, business analysis, and due diligence Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, and Word; Expert proficiency in Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, and Word; knowledge of Capital IQ, Bloomberg, or other data tools is an asset Demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools to enhance financial analysis, data synthesis, and productivity; experience with Capital IQ, Bloomberg, or other data and analytics platforms is considered an asset Strong communication and writing skills with the ability to synthesize complex ideas clearly Curious mindset, strong attention to detail, and a proactive attitude High integrity, professionalism, and team orientation NOTE: This is a full-time contract position (18 months) The expected annual base salary range for this role is: $98,000 - $148,000 CAD The actual base salary offered to the successful candidate may vary based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, individual's expertise and level of experience applicable to the role they are being offered. This job is for an existing vacancy. HOOPP may use artificial intelligence tools to assist in screening, assessing and selecting applicants for this position. These tools support our recruitment process but do not replace human judgment and decision-making.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"hoopp:JR102445","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"R26-99","company_id":"imco","company_name":"IMCO","title":"Associate Portfolio Manager, Public Credit","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Private Credit","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-08","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":135000,"salary_max":176000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://imcoinvest.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/IMCO/job/Toronto---16-York-St/Associate-Portfolio-Manager--Public-Credit_R26-99-1","source_url":"https://imcoinvest.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/IMCO/job/Toronto---16-York-St/Associate-Portfolio-Manager--Public-Credit_R26-99-1","source_name":"IMCO public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Institutional Investing opportunity with IMCO in Toronto, ON focused on Private Credit.","description_text":"At IMCO, our talent is among the best! IMCO offers a uniquely stimulating and rewarding environment where you can help build and drive organizational transformation, all while seeking to challenge yourself, learn, and grow your career. Our culture is built on collaboration and passion, with a shared commitment to delivering lasting value to the clients we serve. Located in downtown Toronto, our vision is to be the partner of choice for Ontario’s public sector funds and to build a high-performing, value-driven asset management firm. This job posting is for an existing vacancy. If you are ready to deliver best-in-class service and join a collaborative, motivated and fun team of professionals, IMCO offers the opportunity to do impactful work and broaden your expertise. If you’re looking to use your expertise to drive strategic outcomes, we’d love to hear from you. ‎ IMCO’s actively managed Global Credit strategy (~$10.1B AUM) delivers higher risk-adjusted returns through a unified approach to credit investing, integrating public and private credit within a single, globally diversified portfolio. The strategy adopts a holistic approach to portfolio construction, allocating across public credit segments, including investment grade, high yield, leveraged loans, and structured credit, alongside private credit segments to capture relative value opportunities, enhance diversification, and optimize liquidity and return outcomes across market cycles. Our collaborative culture and value-add approach to strategic partnerships makes us a preferred partner to some of the largest investors in the world. We have a targeted strategy to grow our highly diversified Global Credit portfolio and are looking for a highly motivated Associate Portfolio Manager to join our Global Credit team with a focus on public credit! The Associate Portfolio Manager, Public Credit will play a key role in managing IMCO’s externally managed Public Credit portfolio, with responsibilities spanning manager selection and due diligence, portfolio strategy and construction, and ongoing monitoring and oversight. The role combines rigorous investment analysis with active portfolio management, while also contributing to ongoing initiatives to enhance the Global Credit platform and target operating model, including the implementation of investment systems and processes and the development of advanced analytics and AI capabilities to improve portfolio insights and support investment decision-making. As a Member of Our Global Credit Team, You Will Contribute Across Three Core Areas: Manager Selection & Oversight, Portfolio Management and Strategy, and Platform Enhancement: Provide analytical and portfolio management support to the Managing Director in overseeing externally managed public credit portfolios on a day-to-day basis, including ad hoc analysis and strategic initiatives. Source, screen, and conduct due diligence on external public credit managers across strategies (e.g., investment grade, high yield, loans and structured credit), utilizing data platforms and AI-enabled tools to analyze performance, identify risks, and support manager screening and ongoing evaluation. Lead and support the preparation of investment recommendations, including drafting investment memos and presentations for internal Investment Committee approval. Assist in structuring and negotiating investment mandates, guidelines, and negotiating fee arrangements with external managers in collaboration with risk, legal and other internal teams. Conduct ongoing monitoring of external managers, including performance attribution, risk exposures, style drift, and adherence to investment guidelines; leverage AI to enhance efficiency in analysis, identify performance and risk trends, and support the development of portfolio-level reporting and insights for senior management. Lead or contribute to initiatives within Global Credit to enhance portfolio management infrastructure through the application of AI and the integration of new investment systems and analytics capabilities; partner with internal teams (Risk, Performance, Operations, Technology) to improve investment data quality to enable more effective analysis, reporting, and decision-making. Support portfolio construction and strategic asset allocation across public credit, including contributing to capital allocation decisions across segments and managers, and shaping overall portfolio strategy. Maintain a strong understanding of global public credit markets, including macroeconomic trends, interest rates, credit spreads, and technical factors, to inform manager selection and portfolio positioning. Engage regularly with external managers through diligence meetings, portfolio reviews, and on-site visits to assess portfolio strategy, market outlook, and execution capabilities. Support client and stakeholder reporting, including preparation of quarterly updates, market commentary, and materials for senior management and board-level discussions. What do you need to succeed? Minimum 5+ years of experience in asset management, with a focus on public credit investing and manager selection and oversight. Experience leveraging data analytics and AI-enabled tools to support investment research, manager evaluation, or portfolio insights. Strong understanding of global public credit markets, including corporate bonds, leveraged loans, structured credit, and credit market dynamics. Experience conducting due diligence on external investment managers, including evaluation of investment processes, portfolio construction, and risk management. Experience in private debt / private credit or broader private markets is considered an asset. Undergraduate degree required. CFA designation, MBA or master’s degree(s) are considered an asset. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to synthesize complex investment information into clear, actionable insights. Effective communicator with the ability to present investment recommendations and market views to senior stakeholders. Collaborative team player with an appreciation for diverse perspectives and a high-performing team environment. Self-starter who can engage and motivate other people around key ideas, effectively listen and provide constructive feedback to others, participate in discussion and brainstorming. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build and maintain relationships with internal teams and external managers. ‎ The base salary range for this position is CAD $135,000.00 - $176,000.00. The placement within the range is determined by the range of market pay for the specific position, as well as the candidate's knowledge, skillset and experience relative to the requirements of the position and to internal peers. In addition to base salary, this position is eligible to participate in IMCO's annual incentive plan. As a candidate, you are encouraged to ask compensation related questions and have an open dialogue with your recruiter who can provide you with the specific details for this position, as well as the total rewards offering at IMCO including our comprehensive benefits package and defined benefit pension plan. ‎ We thank all applicants for their interest. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Our hybrid work model prioritizes an office-first approach, encouraging employees to make the most of our collaborative workspace at 16 York Street, Suite 2400, Toronto, ON M5J 0E6. This welcoming environment fosters teamwork, connection, and professional growth. While flexibility remains a key component of our model, we believe that regular in-office engagement enhances productivity and strengthens our culture. Our approach supports a fulfilling lifestyle that balances professional ambition with personal wellbeing. IMCO is committed to providing accommodation for people with disabilities throughout the recruitment process. If you require support, please let us know and we will work with you to meet your needs. Artificial intelligence (AI) tools may be used to support parts of our recruitment process, such as screening and assessments. However, all hiring decisions are made by our recruitment team. Candidates being considered for this position will be required to undergo background screening.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"imco:R26-99","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR19","company_id":"fengate","company_name":"Fengate Asset Management","title":"Analyst, Real Estate Investments","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Real Estate Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-17","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":85000,"salary_max":100000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://fengate.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/Fengate_Careers/job/Toronto/Analyst--Real-Estate-Investments_JR19","source_url":"https://fengate.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/Fengate_Careers/job/Toronto/Analyst--Real-Estate-Investments_JR19","source_name":"Fengate Asset Management public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Real Estate Investing opportunity with Fengate Asset Management in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"COMPANY OVERVIEW Fengate Asset Management is a leading alternative investment manager focused on infrastructure, private equity, and real estate strategies. Founded in 1974 in Hamilton, Ontario, and with over 250 team members across Canada and the U.S., Fengate is one of the most active real asset and growth equity investors in North America. The firm currently manages over C$10 billion in capital commitments in support of more than C$40 billion in gross asset value, on behalf of over 60 institutional investors across North America, Europe, and Asia. The firm believes that acting responsibly to its stakeholders and communities is fundamental. Fengate is a signatory of both the Institutional Limited Partners Association (ILPA) Diversity in Action initiative and the United Nations-supported Principles for Responsible Investment, integrating environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles into all stages of the firm’s investment process. In 2021, Fengate established its ESG Committee and its EBID (Equity, Belonging, Inclusion and Diversity) Think Tank, consisting of leaders and employees of all backgrounds and levels throughout the firm, to advance and govern the ESG and EBID objectives. Fengate has achieved Platinum Club member status as one of Canada’s Best Managed Companies, retaining this designation since 2007, and has been certified as a Great Place to Work®. Over the past year, Fengate was named one of Canada’s Best Workplaces™ (#4 for companies with 100-999 employees) and as a Best Workplace™ for Financial Services & Insurance, Inclusion, Women, Today’s Youth, Mental Wellness, Giving Back, and Most Trusted Executive Teams. The firm has also been recognized with Waterstone Human Capital’s 2022 Most Admired Corporate Cultures™ award. This program recognizes best-in-class organizations for having cultures that have helped them enhance performance and sustain a competitive advantage. Only 50 organizations are awarded this prestigious corporate culture award each year. OPPORTUNITY Reporting to the Managing Director, Investments, the successful candidate will fill the full time position of Analyst, Real Estate Investments in Toronto. The primary responsibility of this role is to support the acquisition and disposition of a wide range of core, development, and value-add investments in major Canadian cities. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assist in the development, interpretation, and communication of financial models underpinning new and existing land acquisitions related to future development and construction projects. Support the preparation of valuation models for ground-up development projects or repositioning of existing properties (including working with a cross-functional team to compile and analyze operational assumptions, development costs, market research, risk & returns analysis and other topics as required to develop a strong business case for each proposed project). Provide key strategic insights through the use of quantitative and qualitative data (on a location and market-level basis) to inform land acquisitions, development, and project repositioning. Improve upon current, and develop new, tools and templates to streamline and standardize the project evaluation process. Present findings in clear, compelling, and professional presentations to internal and external stakeholders, detailing development feasibility, opportunities, risks, etc. Actively track and report on the progress, timing, and updates on all pipeline projects. Participate in various internal development and investment related meetings. Provide a wide-range of financial and real estate focused analytical support as. KEY QUALIFICATIONS The ideal candidate is highly organized with a keen eye for detail, strong financial acumen, a high level of business maturity and solid decision-making skills University degree in architecture, planning, real-estate development, or business / finance with a real estate emphasis The ideal individual will possess 3 years of varied real estate experience Experience in preparing detailed and professional investment recommendation presentations / reports. Strong Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) skills. Must be self-starter, a strategic thinker and have a service-oriented attitude that will encourage continuous improvement of service and performance. Strong leadership and interpersonal skills with an outstanding level of integrity that will gain the trust and respect of staff and external stakeholders. Demonstrated organizational skills, and the ability to effectively prioritize in a demanding, high paced environment. Ability to formally articulate and present data as requested. CORE COMPETENCIES Being Authentic – Inspiring trust and being courageous. Focusing on Performance – Being accountable and driving results. Understanding Stakeholders – Knowing the needs of those who rely on you. Building Effective Relationships – Collaboration and communication. LOCATION Toronto - Hybrid. PAY RANGE The expected base pay range for this position is: $85,000 - $100,000. Toronto Fengate is an equal opportunity employer, we strive to attract and retain a diverse workforce and are committed to promoting diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in the workplace. It is a core priority at Fengate to create, operate with, and continuously grow and sustain an inclusive culture that respects and connects the diversity of our team, our clients, our partners, and the communities we work in. We are committed to providing accommodation for persons with disabilities. If you require accommodation, we will work with you to meet your needs. We thank all applicants for their interest in this position; however only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"fengate:JR19","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR15","company_id":"fengate","company_name":"Fengate Asset Management","title":"Intern, Private Equity (Summer 2027)","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Intern","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Internship","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-18","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://fengate.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/Fengate_Careers/job/Toronto/Intern--Private-Equity--Summer-2027-_JR15","source_url":"https://fengate.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/Fengate_Careers/job/Toronto/Intern--Private-Equity--Summer-2027-_JR15","source_name":"Fengate Asset Management public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Internship Intern Private Equity opportunity with Fengate Asset Management in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"COMPANY OVERVIEW Fengate Asset Management is a leading alternative investment manager focused on infrastructure, private equity, and real estate strategies. Founded in 1974 in Hamilton, Ontario, and with over 250 team members across Canada and the U.S., Fengate is one of the most active real asset and growth equity investors in North America. The firm currently manages over C$10 billion in capital commitments in support of more than C$40 billion in gross asset value, on behalf of over 60 institutional investors across North America, Europe, and Asia. The firm believes that acting responsibly to its stakeholders and communities is fundamental. Fengate is a signatory of both the Institutional Limited Partners Association (ILPA) Diversity in Action initiative and the United Nations-supported Principles for Responsible Investment, integrating environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles into all stages of the firm’s investment process. In 2021, Fengate established its ESG Committee and its EBID (Equity, Belonging, Inclusion and Diversity) Think Tank, consisting of leaders and employees of all backgrounds and levels throughout the firm, to advance and govern the ESG and EBID objectives. Fengate has achieved Platinum Club member status as one of Canada’s Best Managed Companies, retaining this designation since 2007, and has been certified as a Great Place to Work®. Over the past year, Fengate was named one of Canada’s Best Workplaces™ (#4 for companies with 100-999 employees) and as a Best Workplace™ for Financial Services & Insurance, Inclusion, Women, Today’s Youth, Mental Wellness, Giving Back, and Most Trusted Executive Teams. The firm has also been recognized with Waterstone Human Capital’s 2022 Most Admired Corporate Cultures™ award. This program recognizes best-in-class organizations for having cultures that have helped them enhance performance and sustain a competitive advantage. Only 50 organizations are awarded this prestigious corporate culture award each year. Position & Successful Candidate Profile Company: Fengate Asset Management Title: Intern, Private Equity Reports To: Manager, Private Equity Term: May-August 2027 Location: Toronto OPPORTUNITY As a Private Equity Analyst Intern, you will have a role working with the investment and origination teams within the Private Equity Group. The principal focus of this position will be researching and analyzing a variety of industries and investment opportunities, assisting with the execution of transactions, and supporting the investment team in building strategy initiatives for existing portfolio companies. The role will also expose you to origination activities, financial reporting, tax and compliance related activities within the investments and funds. The position will require the candidate to work with members across the Private Equity team, comprised of 20+ investment, origination, and administration professionals. Fengate is looking for a candidate who has a strong finance foundation coupled with interest and experience in research and investing. Fengate is looking for self-starters, with strong analytical and critical thinking skills, and excellent interpersonal, communications and collaboration skills. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assist the team with building financial models and conducting financial analysis for potential investments. Perform industry (e.g., competitive positioning, SWOT, supply chain, customer segmentation, etc.) and company research and diligence (e.g., operational, financial, commercial) to evaluate potential industries and investments. Assist in preparing investment memorandum materials in Microsoft PowerPoint and Excel . Participate in the ongoing management and performance monitoring of existing portfolio companies, including assisting in the internal valuation process (e.g. precedent and comparable trading analysis). Assist the deal team and portfolio companies’ management teams to implement initiatives and strategic decisions. Assist with the preparation of financial statements, fund reports and investor notices for the respective funds. Manage and maintain the deal pipeline within the Private Equity team’s CRM system, while contributing to ongoing initiatives aimed at enhancing the efficiency and usefulness of the tool. Ad-hoc analysis as well as special projects as required. KEY QUALIFICATIONS Applicant must be an undergraduate student having completed at least 2 years of study in a business/economics program, with excellent academic performance. Applicant must be on track to graduate in 2028/2029. Previous co-op term of meaningful work experience is preferred, ideally in one or more of private equity, principal investing, investment banking, corporate development, capital markets, and/or management consulting. CORE COMPETENCIES Being Authentic – Inspiring trust and being courageous. Focusing on Performance – Being accountable and driving results. Understanding Stakeholders – Knowing the needs of those who rely on you. Building Effective Relationships – Collaboration and communication. Fengate is an equal opportunity employer, we strive to attract and retain a diverse workforce and are committed to promoting diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in the workplace. It is a core priority at Fengate to create, operate with, and continuously grow and sustain an inclusive culture that respects and connects the diversity of our team, our clients, our partners, and the communities we work in. We are committed to providing accommodation for persons with disabilities. If you require accommodation, we will work with you to meet your needs. We thank all applicants for their interest in this position; however only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. Toronto Fengate is an equal opportunity employer, we strive to attract and retain a diverse workforce and are committed to promoting diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in the workplace. It is a core priority at Fengate to create, operate with, and continuously grow and sustain an inclusive culture that respects and connects the diversity of our team, our clients, our partners, and the communities we work in. We are committed to providing accommodation for persons with disabilities. If you require accommodation, we will work with you to meet your needs. We thank all applicants for their interest in this position; however only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"fengate:JR15","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"workbook-27b07956318c3434ddc5","company_id":"clairvest","company_name":"Clairvest","title":"Associate - Private Equity at Clairvest","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Private Equity","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":null,"program_type":null,"term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":null,"application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/search-results/","source_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/search-results/","source_name":"Clairvest public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Private Equity opportunity with Clairvest in Toronto, ON focused on Private Equity.","description_text":null,"description_status":"missing","description_verified_at":null,"source_record_id":"clairvest:workbook-27b07956318c3434ddc5","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"2238","company_id":"upp","company_name":"University Pension Plan Ontario","title":"Senior Analyst, Private Equity","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Private Credit","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":null,"program_type":null,"term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":null,"application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/upp/ExternalCANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/2238","source_url":"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/upp/ExternalCANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/2238","source_name":"University Pension Plan Ontario public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Private Equity opportunity with University Pension Plan Ontario in Toronto, ON focused on Private Credit.","description_text":null,"description_status":"missing","description_verified_at":null,"source_record_id":"upp:2238","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR5966","company_id":"ci-financial","company_name":"CI Financial","title":"Investment Analyst","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Asset Management","specialization":"Public Credit / Fixed Income","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":null,"program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":null,"application_deadline":null,"salary_min":115000,"salary_max":140000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://ci.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CI_FINANCIAL_EXTERNAL_CAREER-SITE/job/Toronto-ON/Investment-Analyst_JR5966","source_url":"https://ci.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CI_FINANCIAL_EXTERNAL_CAREER-SITE/job/Toronto-ON/Investment-Analyst_JR5966","source_name":"CI Financial public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Asset Management opportunity with CI Financial in Toronto, ON focused on Public Credit / Fixed Income.","description_text":"At CI, we see a great place to work as one that is a safe place for everyone to have a voice, where people are empowered to take ownership over meaningful work, where there is an opportunity to grow through stretching themselves, where they can work on innovative products and projects, and where employees are supported and engaged in doing so. The Financials equity research team is looking to add an Investment Analyst who can support fundamental investment research while also helping the team become more efficient and technology-enabled. The ideal candidate is a fundamental investor with strong technology fluency. They should understand stocks, financial statements, valuation, and capital markets, while also being naturally inclined to identify inefficient processes and improve them through better tools, data organization, automation, and AI-enabled workflows. The successful candidate will work closely with senior members of the Financials team and portfolio managers, supporting research across banks, insurance companies, asset managers, exchanges, fintech companies, and other financial institutions. WHAT YOU WILL DO Financials Research Conduct industry and competitive analysis. Build and maintain financial models and valuation frameworks. Analyze quarterly earnings results and management commentary. Assist in the development of investment recommendations and research reports. Monitor company developments and identify potential investment opportunities. Participate in meetings with company management teams and industry experts. Support coverage of banks, insurance companies, asset managers, exchanges, fintech companies and other financial institutions. Research Innovation & Technology Bring a technology-aware and improvement-oriented mindset to the research process. Identify opportunities to make recurring research tasks, information gathering, and team workflows more efficient. Use available technology, data tools, and AI-enabled capabilities thoughtfully to support analysis and productivity. Contribute ideas for improving research organization, information retrieval, and collaboration across the team. Partner with internal technology, data, and research-support resources to help assess and implement larger-scale solutions where appropriate. Stay informed on relevant developments in data, analytics, automation, and AI that may have practical applications for investment research.\" WHAT YOU WILL BRING Required 1-3 years of experience in equity research, investment management, investment banking, capital markets, or related fields. Strong interest in equity investing and security analysis. Understanding of financial statements and valuation concepts. Excellent analytical and communication skills. Advanced Excel proficiency. Demonstrated curiosity and desire to learn. Preferred Interest in financial institutions and capital markets. Progress toward the CFA designation. Experience applying AI tools to research, data analysis, or workflow automation. Familiarity with Bloomberg, FactSet, Capital IQ, or similar platforms. Experience with Python, SQL, VBA, Power BI, or similar tools. This role follows our in office work model and requires employees to be onsite four days per week to support collaboration and business needs. This opportunity is for an existing vacancy with the company. The anticipated base salary range for this position is $115,000 to $140,000. Exact salary depends on several factors such as experience, skills, education, and budget. Salary range may vary based on geographic location. In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for participation in a bonus program. In addition, The Company offers a variety of benefits to eligible employees, including health insurance coverage, wellness programs, life and disability insurance, retirement savings plans, paid leave programs, education-related programs, paid holidays and vacation time, and many others. Many of these benefits are subsidized or fully paid for by the company. CI Financial is an independent company offering global wealth management and asset management advisory services through diverse financial services firms. Since 1965, we have consistently anticipated and responded to the changing needs of investors. We are driven by a commitment to provide individuals and institutions with the highest-quality investments and advice. Our commitment to the highest levels of performance means that whatever their position, CI employees must be comfortable in a fast-paced environment that will stretch them to tap into their highest potential. Employees with a healthy dose of ambition, a desire to commit to a curious mindset for continuous learning, and a willingness to go the extra mile thrive at CI. A Supportive Environment for Success We offer an in-office environment, competitive benefits, and a supportive workplace to help our employees thrive both personally and professionally. WHAT WE OFFER Modern HQ location within walking distance from Union Station Training Reimbursement Paid Professional Designations Employee Savings Plan (ESP) Corporate Discount Program Enhanced group benefits Parental Leave Top–up program Paid time off for Volunteering We are focused on building a diverse and inclusive workforce. If you are excited about this role and are not confident you meet all the qualification requirements, we encourage you to apply to investigate the opportunity further. Please submit your resume in confidence by clicking “Apply”. Only qualified candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. CI Financial Corp. and all of our affiliates (“CI”) are committed to fair and accessible employment practices and provide reasonable accommodations for persons with disabilities. If you require accommodations in order to apply for any job opportunities, require this posting in an additional format, or require accommodation at any stage of the recruitment process please contact us at accessible.recruitment@ci.com, or call 416-364-1145 ext. 4747.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","source_record_id":"ci-financial:JR5966","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility. Career-path classification depends on metadata or description text.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"R2052799","company_id":"brookfield-asset-management","company_name":"Brookfield Asset Management","title":"Investment Associate, Private Equity","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":null,"program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":null,"application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://brookfield.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/brookfield/job/Toronto-Ontario/Investment-Associate--Private-Equity_R2052799","source_url":"https://brookfield.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/brookfield/job/Toronto-Ontario/Investment-Associate--Private-Equity_R2052799","source_name":"Brookfield Asset Management public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Private Equity opportunity with Brookfield Asset Management in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":null,"description_status":"missing","description_verified_at":null,"source_record_id":"brookfield-asset-management:R2052799","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T02:31:18.723Z"},{"external_job_id":"5254348008","company_id":"canada-infrastructure-bank","company_name":"Canada Infrastructure Bank","title":"Analyst, Investments (Bilingual)","location_di